From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5kjn5: use the pinned kernel pad callback API

The original v6 driver targets next-20260925. The phone's fixed
7a81d184e309 kernel uses the preceding three-argument pad callbacks.
Remove the unused client-info parameter from set_fmt/get_selection so
both callbacks match the actual v4l2_subdev_pad_ops definitions. Keep
the public sensor mode/register tables and all runtime behavior unchanged.

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn5.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5kjn5.c
@@ -2673,7 +2673,6 @@
 }
 
 static int s5kjn5_set_fmt(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
-			  const struct v4l2_subdev_client_info *ci,
 			  struct v4l2_subdev_state *state,
 			  struct v4l2_subdev_format *fmt)
 {
@@ -2689,7 +2688,6 @@
 }
 
 static int s5kjn5_get_selection(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
-				const struct v4l2_subdev_client_info *ci,
 				struct v4l2_subdev_state *state,
 				struct v4l2_subdev_selection *sel)
 {
